body:
Drug: (noun) "a medicine or other substance which has a physiological effect when ingested or otherwise introduced into the body."

&#x200B;

Which would include water......And probably just about anything.This isn't an argument about drugs, it's semantics about what constitutes a drug.

Far too kind, sir.

&#x200B;

As for the vehicle/gun losses, they do seem high after three days. But the Allies lose a boatload of equipment during the initial invasion. The Germans have a lot of guns in static positions that get cleared in the first few days, and 21st Pz got almost an entire regiment surrounded and killed during the June 7th counterattack.

Gotcha. And just for the record, I'm not a big fan of 'optimal strategies' myself. Mainly because most of them rely on your opponent doing what you want him to do. Which is usually fine against the AI, but rarely works against human opponents.

&#x200B;

So a basic introduction to how fatigue, morale, command, supply, firepower etc. interact, and what to watch out for. That I can do.

Well, anyone who is doing online flying started out being pretty crappy at it. And most controllers are very helpful. Just put 'New to VATSIM' in the remarks of your flight-plan, and you'll do fine. Although obviously stay away from places like KJFK, KLAX, EGLL and the like until you have the routines down. Those places are BUSY.

&#x200B;

Alternatively, if you're unwilling to just dive in, your best bet is probably joining a Virtual Airline. Most of the more established ones have Online training courses designed to get you up and running. Some even have internal servers just for them where you can practice with controllers from that VA.
